OpenVDDK: match VMware's VDDK ABI where nbdkit's vddk plugin depends on it

Found when nbdkit 1.38 (vddk plugin) segfaulted opening any disk:

1. VixDiskLib_AllocateConnectParams took an out-parameter and returned an
   error code. VMware's signature is
   `VixDiskLibConnectParams *VixDiskLib_AllocateConnectParams(void)`, so
   callers got 0 back as the struct pointer and wrote through NULL.
2. VixDiskLibConnectParams lacked reserved3/reserved4/reserved5 and placed
   specType before spec. Callers write specType at offset 120, past the end
   of the 112-byte struct OpenVDDK allocated.
3. VixDiskLib_FreeConnectParams freed the strings inside the struct.
   VMware's frees only the struct; callers own those strings (nbdkit points
   them at its own config buffers), so this was an invalid free.
4. VixDiskLibDiskInfo lacked uuid/logicalSectorSize/physicalSectorSize,
   which callers read when the library reports version >= 7 (OpenVDDK
   reports 8).
5. ReadAsync/WriteAsync returned VIX_OK for a queued request. VMware returns
   VIX_ASYNC and delivers the result to the callback; nbdkit fails every
   read otherwise ("VixDiskLib_ReadAsync: The operation was successful").

Static assertions pin the LP64 offsets so a regression fails the build.

